{
  "recordId": "chemie-current439-HB-primary232-informed-independent-b-20261017-v1.inventory",
  "runId": "chemie-current439-HB-primary232-informed-independent-b-20261017-v1",
  "verdict": "revise",
  "findings": [
    {
      "findingId": "HB232-B-01",
      "frozenReasoning": "### HB232-B-01 — E4 purpose/scope — REVISE\n\nSourceGoal `hb-chemistry-sekii-gyo2022-clause-p09-std-e-standard-e1-e12-gk_lk-04`; clause `HB2022-p09-STD-E-standard-E1-E12-GK_LK-04`; physical/printed page9, E4.\n\nThe current sourceText/parentBulletText/title/description read as planning investigations **including hypothesis testing**. The original E4 plans experimental or model-based approaches, with variable control where appropriate, **also** for testing hypotheses, statements or theories. It does not make hypothesis testing the sole specified purpose of all such planning. The current operator list `planen` does not restore the omitted objects or the original additive qualification. Restore the breadth and the 'auch' relationship, including statements and theories; do not turn every investigation plan into mandatory hypothesis testing or require every task to test all three categories. The current conditional treatment of variable control is otherwise sound. Update the corresponding page9 authored passage when revising this body.\n"
    },
    {
      "findingId": "HB232-B-02",
      "frozenReasoning": "### HB232-B-02 — E12 example status — REVISE\n\nSourceGoal `hb-chemistry-sekii-gyo2022-clause-p09-std-e-standard-e1-e12-gk_lk-12`; clause `HB2022-p09-STD-E-standard-E1-E12-GK_LK-12`; physical/printed page9, E12.\n\nThe original requires reflection on the possibilities and limits of the concrete inquiry process and the knowledge obtained, and gives reproducibility, falsifiability, intersubjectivity, logical consistency and provisionality as **examples**. The current paraphrase instead specifies reflection 'hinsichtlich' the five named properties, with no example marker and no explicit original possibilities/limits framing. This can turn an illustrative parenthesis into a fixed five-part evidence quota. Preserve the central process/results scope and mark these dimensions as examples rather than an exhaustive mandatory checklist. No new competency or new source clause is needed; the clause identity remains the same. Update its page9 authored passage too.\n"
    },
    {
      "findingId": "HB232-B-03",
      "frozenReasoning": "### HB232-B-03 — B13 assessment objects — REVISE\n\nSourceGoal `hb-chemistry-sekii-gyo2022-clause-p12-std-b-standard-b2-b14-gk_lk-12`; clause `HB2022-p12-STD-B-standard-B2-B14-GK_LK-12`; physical/printed page12, B13.\n\nThe current paraphrase names consequences of chemical products, methods and one's own actions. The original B13 additionally explicitly names **Verfahren** and **Erkenntnisse**, alongside products and methods, while retaining one's own actions and ecological/economic/social sustainability perspectives. The current B12 row does retain all four chemical objects, so the omission in B13 cannot be dismissed as a consistent umbrella terminology policy. Its operator metadata lists only assessment verbs and does not restore the missing objects. Restore procedures/processes and knowledge/findings in B13's source body and corresponding page12 passage. Both original assessment operators, the three sustainability perspectives and own action are already preserved.\n"
    }
  ],
